      "title": "Career Opportunities: Juriste",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Juriste (22962) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Juriste (22962) Requisition ID 22962 - Posted 09/01/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 17’000 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. unil.ch/travailler Présentation Pour compléter son équipe, le service juridique de l’UNIL est à la recherche d'un·e juriste Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : immédiate ou date à convenir Durée du contrat : Durée indéterminée Taux d'activité : 80% Lieu de travail : Lausanne-Unicentre Vos activités Dans le cadre de votre activité vous serez amené(e) à : Gérer et coordonner les procédures de recours dans le domaine de la formation Conseiller les membres de la Direction de l’UNIL dans le cadre des procédures disciplinaires, gérer et coordonner les procédures Conseiller et orienter juridiquement les services, facultés ainsi que toute entité au bénéfice des prestations délivrées par le service juridique Contribuer à la rédaction ou à la révision des directives et règlements et assurer leur conformité légale Gérer les projets qui vous sont confiés par la hiérarchie et assurer leur coordination Votre profil Vous bénéficiez d’un master en droit suisse et de 3 à 5 ans d’expérience professionnelle dans des activités juridiques liées au poste ; le brevet d’avocat est un atout Vous appréciez la diversité d’activités et disposez d’un intérêt marqué pour le droit public et la procédure administrative Vous disposez d’excellentes capacités à mener des projets complexes, à mettre des priorités, à identifier et anticiper les risques et faites preuve d’une bonne résistance au stress tout en restant pragmatique et clair Vos compétences sociales sont reconnues et vous savez vous adapter à différentes situations et interlocuteurs Vous connaissez le milieu académique et ses enjeux ou êtes intéressé à les découvrir Pour vous l’esprit d’équipe, le partage de connaissances et de points de vue est source d’enrichissement et de plaisir au travail Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié. Des possibilités de formation continue, une multitude d'activités et d'autres avantages à découvrir. Davantage d'informations sur unil.ch/travailler Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Gwenaëlle Gilliéron Directrice du service juridique gwenaelle.gillieron@unil.ch 021/692.20.04 Votre dossier de candidature Délai de postulation : 22.09.2026 Nous vous invitons à nous transmettre votre dossier complet en format Word ou PDF. Il ne sera pris en compte que les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site. Nous vous remercions de votre compréhension. Cahier des charges du poste Cliquez ici pour afficher le cahier des charges. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie. unil.ch/egalite unil.ch/familles Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22942&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=iIWRoMDzoWInBntlWN%2btI%2b5QvEUbX8zhy8R5PKoLxfI%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry (22942) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: PhD position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry (22942) Requisition ID 22942 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Institute of Earth Surface Dynamics ( IDYST ) is inviting applications for a fully-funded Ph.D position in Experimental Soil Hydrogeochemistry within the Hydrology group (Principal Investigator : Prof. Paolo Benettin). Job information Expected start date in position : 01.01.2027/ to be agreed Contract length : 1 year initially, extension up to 4 years Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Lausanne Mouline (Géopolis building) Your responsibilities The Ph.D. candidate will design and perform a series of experiments at the Unil Ecotron facility , to investigate how vegetation regulates soil water fluxes and geochemical reactions , expecially during dry periods. The facility already includes a programmable climate chamber with three soil columns and a range of sensors, and additional sensors can be acquired during the project. Depending on the candidate's interests and skills, the work may combine a range of methods, including analyses of major and trace elements, measurements of vegetation activity, tracer experiments and hydrogeochemical modelling. As climate change increases the frequency and severity of droughts, this Ph.D. project offers the opportunity to understand and anticipate drought impacts on water resources and ecosystem degradation, while developing expertise at the interface of hydrology, soil geochemistry, and ecosystem science. 80% of the employment time will be dedicated to completing the doctoral thesis (PhD research); the remaining 20% will be dedicated to teaching assistant and support duties within the institute. You are expected to : Design and conduct innovative experiments Operate the Ecotron facility and its network of ~80 sensors throughout the project Lead scientific articles in international peer-reviewed journals Participate in international conferences and project meetings in lausanne and Paris Participate in approximately one week of fieldwork per year at the Critical Zone Observatory of Mt Lozère, France Make your research workflow (data, code, protocols...) open and reproducible Openly discuss research obstacles and seek advice/help in the group Actively participate in creating a collaborative and inclusive culture Your qualifications Background in disciplines like Environmental Science, Soil Science/Physics, Biogeochemistry, Experimental Ecology, Hydrology, Civil/Environmental Engineering, or closely related disciplines. Previous experience with experimental work. Examples may include deploying sensors, collecting soil/water/vegetation samples from the field, conducting laboratory analyses. Strong quantitative and data handling skills (e.g. in R or Python). Good written and spoken English communication skills. Knowledge of French is an asset but is not required. What the position offers you Annual salary of CHF 55'000 for up to 4 years (until graduation). A friendly and cohesive culture at the Institute of Earth Surface Dynamics ( IDYST ) including 1-day Summer and Winter retreats, usually in the Alps. A shared office in the pleasent Géopolis building, on campus. Fully-funded personal research equipment (laptop, desktop computer, monitor, etc.) and research-related travel (conferences, collaborations, etc.). Opportunity for co-supervision of the Ph.D. program by a second Principal Ingestigator. International collaboration network and opportunities to spend research periods abroad. Opportunity (but not obligation) to attend doctoral schools and take classes. Access to laboratories and platforms (analytical platform, geochemistry, stable isotopes) as well as workshops (wood, metal, 3D print). Support in your future career choices, throug the IDYST Careers group and Graduate Campus activities. Access to Unil Campus facilities (Sports center with 100+ recreational options, restaurants, etc). 5 weeks of paid holidays (in addition to 1 week of national holidays) and Paid Parental leave . The University of Lausanne is committed to equal opportunity and stands firm against all forms of discrimination. The Faculty of Geosciences and Environment of the University of Lausanne adheres to the DORA agreement and follows its guidelines in the evaluation of applications (in short-quality over quantity). Contact for further information All questions related to the application can be adressed by email to the Unil Hydrology Group : hydrology@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 30.09.2026 Please, send the following document in PDF format : Motivation letter (strict max 2 pages), including : Your professional goals in the next 6-7 years, and how this position might further them A ~250-word description of a topic you felt passionate about in the last ~2 years Description of the methods you feel more comfortable with and why (e.g. numerical modeling, sensor deployment, sample collection, lab analysis, statistics, spatial analyses, programming, etc.) A disclosure of how Artificial Intelligence was used to prepare your application Short Curriculum Vitae (max 2 pages) Copy of all university degree certificates and transcripts Copy of one first-author research report (can be a manuscript, a thesis, or an assignment report) Names, affiliations, and emails addresses of at least 2 references (e.g. Master thesis advisor, academic staff who have read your work, previous employers) Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
