    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22979&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=xbCEUEpIkQQqUk9sDJZOJWffJjZ4YPiTPo50Ej8w%2fYg%3d": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in deep learning for protein structure, interactions & design (22979) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in deep learning for protein structure, interactions & design (22979) Requisition ID 22979 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation We develop deep learning and computational methods to understand and design proteins and their interactions. We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to develop and lead a research direction within the group. Our research interests include: ● representation learning from protein foundation models ● biomolecular structure and interaction prediction, including protein-ligand and protein-protein interactions ● generative protein design ● generalisable deep learning for biomolecular systems ● remote homology detection and large-scale functional analysis For an overview of our research, see pickybinders.org . These are broad directions, you will have substantial freedom to shape your research within the group. Job information Duration: 2 years (initial contract for 1 year, but funding is available for 2 years) Potential for further extension depending on funding Start date: Earliest November 2026, by arrangement Workplace: University of Lausanne, Dorigny Your qualifications We are looking for ● A PhD (completed or near completion) in machine learning, computer science, computational biology, or a related field ● Strong Python skills and experience with a deep learning framework (PyTorch preferred) ● Experience applying deep learning to structured or scientific data ● A track record of research through publications, preprints, or open-source software ● Independence, curiosity, and the ability to develop and pursue new research ideas Prior experience with proteins or structural biology is useful but not required. We welcome applicants from adjacent areas including generative modelling, representation learning, language models, and geometric deep learning who are interested in applying their expertise to protein science Contact for further question Prof Janani Durairaj, e-mail: janani.durairaj@unil.ch Your application Deadline: ongoing Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. ● a CV including publications, preprints, and relevant software ● a 1–2 page letter describing your previous research, the scientific problems that currently interest you, how these connect to the group, and why you are applying ● the names of two refereesApplications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. We encourage applications from candidates from backgrounds underrepresented in computational science Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22980&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=xbCEUEpIkQQqUk9sDJZOJWffJjZ4YPiTPo50Ej8w%2fYg%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: PhD student position in deep learning for enzyme structure & catalysis",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: PhD student position in deep learning for enzyme structure & catalysis (22980) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: PhD student position in deep learning for enzyme structure & catalysis (22980) Requisition ID 22980 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation We’re looking for a PhD student to develop deep learning methods for modelling biomolecular interactions in the context of catalysis. Protein–ligand cofolding models aim to jointly predict protein structures and the binding poses of small molecules. Enzyme catalysis presents a different challenge: molecular interactions need to be understood in the context of the chemical reaction being catalysed and the dynamics of the changes involved. The project will investigate how protein–ligand cofolding approaches can be extended to better model enzymes and their reactions, with a particular interest in methods that generalise across enzyme families and chemical transformations. The project will combine deep learning, protein bioinformatics, and large-scale analysis of protein sequences, structures and biochemical data. There will be scope to explore model development and evaluation, representation learning, and applications to catalytic function and molecular design. For an overview of our research interests, see pickybinders.org. Job information Start date in position: Earliest November 2026, by arrangement Contract length : 1 year, renewable, maximum 5 years Activity rate : 100% Workplace : University of Lausanne, Dorigny campus Your qualifications We are looking for ● A Master's degree in computer science, computational biology, bioinformatics, machine learning, chemistry, biochemistry, or a related field ● Good programming skills, preferably in Python ● An interest in machine learning and proteins ● Curiosity about the relationship between molecular sequence, structure and biochemical function ● Motivation to develop and pursue research ideas independently, and to learn new subjects and techniques. Experience with deep learning, structural biology, cheminformatics, or protein bioinformatics is useful but not required. We do not expect applicants to already have expertise across all of these areas. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Prof. Janani Durairaj, e-mail: janani.durairaj@unil.ch Your application Deadline : ongoing Please, send your full application as a single PDF document comprising: ● a CV ● a short cover letter describing your research interests, relevant experience, and why you are interested in the project ● the names of two referees Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. We encourage applications from candidates from backgrounds underrepresented in computational science Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22967&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=xbCEUEpIkQQqUk9sDJZOJWffJjZ4YPiTPo50Ej8w%2fYg%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Post-doctoral position in the neurobiology of anesthesia in Drosophila",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Post-doctoral position in the neurobiology of anesthesia in Drosophila (22967) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Post-doctoral position in the neurobiology of anesthesia in Drosophila (22967) Requisition ID 22967 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction The University of Lausanne (UNIL) is a higher teaching and research institution composed of seven faculties where around 15,000 students and 5,000 researchers, collaborators, and professors work and study. Situated along the shores of Lake Léman, near Lausanne’s city centre, its campuses bring together over 120 nationalities. Presentation Prof. Richard Benton ( www.unil.ch/cig/benton ) at the Center for Integrative Genomics at UNIL is seeking a post-doctoral researcher with a strong background in Drosophila behavioural neurogenetics and calcium imaging. Job information Expected start date in position : 01.04.2027 Contract length : 1 year, renewable Activity rate : 100% Workplace : University of Lausanne, Dorigny Campus Your responsibilities Volatile anesthetics (VAs) are essential in medicine, yet their precise mechanisms of action remain unclear. Initially thought to act broadly on lipid membranes, later studies implicated ion channels such as GABA-A and glutamate receptors as some of their molecular targets. However, no single molecular target explains the full spectrum of anesthetic effects, suggesting contribution of additional factors. Drosophila melanogaster offers a powerful model for dissecting genetic and physiological contributors to VA sensitivity. We have recently initiated a new project using a genome-wide association study approach to identified novel genetic factors defiing sensitivity to different VAs. You will contribute to this work by performing whole-brain calcium imaging to explore the effects on different VAs on the activity of different brain region, and genetic manipulations to characteristic candidate molecular targets. Although most of your time will be dedicated to your research project, you will also be involved in undergraduate teaching (e.g., practical class preparation, literature reading classes). Your qualifications A PhD degree in biology Strong interests and skills in genetics and neurobiology Extensive experience in Drosophila culture, quantitative behavioural analysis and calcium imaging Excellent scientific writing, communication and interpersonal skills, self-motivation and independence What the position offers you You will be supervised by Prof. Richard Benton, in a diverse, dynamic and international research laboratory. The working language is English. The Center for Integrative Genomics encompasses 14 research labs investigating diverse fields related to functional genomics and offers state-of-the-art experimental facilities. Beyond the training in the host laboratory, numerous possibilities exist at UNIL for further professional education (e.g., in bioinformatics, imaging, soft-skills, career development). Contact for further information Informal requests for information can be made by email to: Richard.Benton@unil.ch Your application To apply you must upload as a single pdf document: a CV, including the name and contact details of 2-3 referees a motivation letter in English describing (i) your past research experience and accomplishments, and (ii) your scientific interests, and how they are a good match for the host laboratory and project Deadline : 30.09.2026 Only applications through the University of Lausanne job portal will be taken into account (this website). Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22974&selected_lang=fr_FR&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=xbCEUEpIkQQqUk9sDJZOJWffJjZ4YPiTPo50Ej8w%2fYg%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Stagiaire pour le Festival Fécule",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Stagiaire pour le Festival Fécule (22974) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter Career Opportunities: Stagiaire pour le Festival Fécule (22974) Requisition ID 22974 - Posted 09/15/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 17’000 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. unil.ch/travailler Présentation Le Service Culture et Médiation scientifique (SCMS) vise à partager les savoirs académiques avec le grand public, stimuler la réflexion, la curiosité et le dialogue avec les citoyen·ne·s. Au travers de différents programmes culturels et de médiation scientifique portés par ses deux marques phares - L’éprouvette (Laboratoire Sciences et Société de l’UNIL) et La Grange (Centre Arts et Sciences de l’UNIL), il contribue au développement et à l’enrichissement de la vie scientifique, culturelle et artistique de la région. Le Service Culture et Médiation scientifique de l’Université de Lausanne met au concours un poste de : Stagiaire pour le Festival Fécule Votre mission En étroite collaboration avec la chargée de projet du Festival Fécule, vous participez à la gestion des aspects administratifs et organisationnels du Festival et à la mise en place des actions de communication et de médiation culturelle. L’édition 2027 du Festival Fécule aura lieu du 3 au 15 mai 2027 et est l’occasion pour plus de 300 étudiantexs, collaborateuricexs ou associations (en provenance de l’UNIL, de l’EPFL et d’autres universités) de présenter leur travail artistique dans un théâtre professionnel. Le festival rythme la vie du campus en se déployant au plateau de La Grange, au Nucleo en passant par des propositions en extérieur. Bords de plateau et projets de médiation sont mis à l’honneur, afin de prolonger l’expérience au-delà des représentations. Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : 1er novembre 2026 Durée du contrat : 7 mois (CDD) Taux d’activité : 10% du 1er novembre 2026 au 31 mai 2027 , avec une augmentation à 80% du 1er au 15 mai 2027 Lieu de travail : UNIL – Dorigny Stage rémunéré selon les barèmes de l’UNIL : lien vers les barèmes Votre profil •    Formation universitaire de niveau bachelor ou master souhaitée ; •    Bon sens de l’organisation et de la planification ; •    Excellente maîtrise orale et écrite du français ; •    Aisance relationnelle et entregent ; •    Intérêt marqué pour les milieux culturels. Conditions du poste Poste à 10%, avec une augmentation à 80% pendant les deux semaines du Festival Fécule 2027, afin de soutenir l’organisation et le bon déroulement des événements. Votre dossier de candidature Votre dossier comprendra une lettre de motivation et un CV, copie de diplômes et certificats de travail. Il ne sera pris en compte que les candidatures adressées par le biais du site UNIL / offres d'emplois Délai de candidature : 20 septembre 2026. Renseignements complémentaires Service Culture et Médiation scientifique Romane Dussez, Chargée de projet / Festival Fécule : romane.dussez(a)unil.ch Cahier des charges du poste Cliquez ici pour afficher le cahier des charges. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage pour l’égalité. www.unil.ch/egalite L’UNIL soutient la relève scientifique. www.unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
