    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22935&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=TXPXZNKdXQyAAVvP%2b9nxJIAmMdiPvLmW22ci1exLsFs%3d": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Lab Manager - Genomic Technologies Facility (22935) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Lab Manager - Genomic Technologies Facility (22935) Requisition ID 22935 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The mission of the Genomic Technologies Facility (GTF) is to provide users with shared access to state-of-the-art genomics technologies , as well as advanced support for experimental design, project execution, and data analysis. The team consists of around ten scientists working across both laboratory and data analysis activities. These activities include the production of genomic data using established protocols, as well as the d evelopment—design and optimization - of new methodological approaches . In this context, the Laboratory Manager will support users in the design and execution of genomics projects by providing scientific and technical expertise tailored to their research needs. The successful candidate will oversee the day-to-day follow-up of laboratory activities, coordinate the resources required for service delivery, and help ensure the smooth execution of platform operations. They will also contribute to the continuous improvement of the facility's services, processes, and infrastructure to meet the evolving needs of the scientific community. Job information Expected start date in position : To be agreed Contract length : Undetermined Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Quartier Sorge, Génopode Your responsibilities Advise users on the design, planning, and execution of genomics projects. Evaluate experimental requirements and recommend the most appropriate methodological and technological approaches. Oversee the delivery of platform services and coordinate the laboratory activities required for their execution. Ensure the proper operation and follow-up of laboratory equipment and infrastructure. Serve as a point of contact for users regarding project progress and technical aspects of the services provided. Contribute to maintaining the platform's quality, and traceability standards. Support the management of laboratory resources, including equipment, consumables, and maintenance activities. Identify and implement improvements to laboratory procedures, services, and organization. Your qualifications Extensive hands-on experience in high-throughput sequencing and genomics technologies, acquired within a genomics core facility, service platform, or a comparable environment. Recognized expertise in genomics technologies, with extensive practical experience operating and supporting short-read and long-read sequencing platforms in a research or core facility environment. Strong understanding of laboratory workflows, quality management principles, and operational requirements associated with a high-throughput genomics facility. Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills, with a strong service-oriented mindset and the ability to interact effectively with researchers from diverse scientific backgrounds. Master's degree or PhD in Life Sciences or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of advanced training and relevant experience, together with substantial experience in genomics technologies and platform operations. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information For any specific enquiries, please contact: Julien Marquis, Head of Genomic Technologies Facility, julien.marquis.1@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 02.10.2026 Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Job description Click here to open the job description. Additional information Niveaux 1 à 12 : UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families Niveaux 13 et + : UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance. In order to increase the number of women in management positions, applications from women are particularly encouraged. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22943&selected_lang=en_US&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=TXPXZNKdXQyAAVvP%2b9nxJIAmMdiPvLmW22ci1exLsFs%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position: Pathogen sensing, innate immunity and autoimmunity",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position: Pathogen sensing, innate immunity and autoimmunity (22943) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position: Pathogen sensing, innate immunity and autoimmunity (22943) Requisition ID 22943 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation A Postdoctoral position is available in the laboratory of Prof. Manuele Rebsamen at the Department of Immunobiology, University of Lausanne, Switzerland. The Rebsamen lab investigates the signaling pathways and metabolic processes that allow immune cells to detect and respond to invading pathogens, and their implication in autoimmune diseases. We are seeking an enthusiastic candidate to investigate the mechanisms and regulatory processes controlling innate immune responses, and their role in antimicrobial responses and autoimmunity . Additional information: www.rebsamenlab.org Selected publications (# corresponding authors): Heinz, …, Rebsamen# & Superti-Furga#. TASL is the SLC15A4-associated adaptor for IRF5 activation by TLR7-9 . Nature. 2020; Bernaleau, …, Rebsamen. CCDC134 controls TLR biogenesis through the ER-chaperone Gp96 . Journal of Experimental Medicine, 2025 Drobek, ..., Rebsamen. TLR7-9 adaptors TASL and TASL2 mediate IRF5-dependent antiviral responses and autoimmunity . Nature Communications, 2025 Drobek, ..., Rebsamen. The SLC15A4-TASL complex is essential for lupus development in mice. Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 2026 (accepted) Job information Expected start date in position: From January 1st, 2027 or to be agreed. Contract duration: 1 year, with the possibility of renewal for a maximum total of 5 years Employment rate: 100% Place of work: Dpt. of Immunobiology, UNIL, Ch. des Boveresses 155,1066 Epalinges, Switzerland Your responsibilities In your activities, you will have to: Lead a research project Contribute to collaborative team projects Contribute to the supervision of students Your qualifications In order to expand our team, we are looking for candidates with the following skills: Ph.D. in a relevant discipline, e.g. immunology or molecular biology Enthusiasm for science, self-motivation and a strong interest in immunology Motivation to collaborate and work in a team At least one 1st author research publication Eligibility for postdoctoral fellowships (e.g. EMBO or similar) Strong spoken and written competency in English (French is not necessary) What the position offers you We offer a competitive, funded research project and a nice working place in a multicultural and dynamic academic environment. The working language is English. The laboratory is located at the Epalinges campus, a creative and inspiring environment with strengths in immunology, infectious diseases and cancer, which hosts the Dpt. of Immunobiology as well as laboratories from the University Hospital (CHUV) and the Ludwig Cancer Research Institute. The campus offers multiple state-of-the-art research facilities. Contact for further information Prof. Manuele Rebsamen: manuele.rebsamen@unil.ch ; Your application Deadline: 20.09.2026 (applications will be assessed upon submission) Applications should be submitted as a single PDF in English and include: A cover letter including a description of your research experience and motivation (1.5 pages max) A curriculum vitae including a list of publications Names and contact information of three academic references Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career%5fns=job%5flisting&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB%5fSEARCH&rcm%5fsite%5flocale=en%5fUS&career_job_req_id=22972&selected_lang=fr_FR&jobAlertController_jobAlertId=&jobAlertController_jobAlertName=&browserTimeZone=America/Los_Angeles&_s.crb=TXPXZNKdXQyAAVvP%2b9nxJIAmMdiPvLmW22ci1exLsFs%3d": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities: Assistant·e diplômé·e suppléant·e en sciences du sport",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Assistant·e diplômé·e suppléant·e en sciences du sport - physiologie musculaire (22972) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Assistant·e diplômé·e suppléant·e en sciences du sport - physiologie musculaire (22972) Requisition ID 22972 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (2) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 15’500 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny, et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. www.unil.ch/carrieres Présentation L'Institut des sciences du sport (ISSUL) de l’Université de Lausanne met au concours un poste de Assistant·e diplômé·e suppléant·e en sciences du sport – physiologie musculaire Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : 01 décembre 2026 Durée du contrat : 6 mois Taux d'activité : 100% Lieu de travail : Lausanne-Dorigny Salaire annuel brut : CHF 67'568, en progression chaque année selon le barème Vos activités Le poste est placé sous la responsabilité du professeur Nicolas Place. Il est attendu du ou de la titulaire qu’il ou elle réalise / poursuive les travaux en cours portant sur la plasticité de la fonction musculaire. Une contribution aux activités d’enseignement à l’ISSUL est également attendue. 50% du taux d’activité sera dédié aux travaux de recherche personnels. 21% du taux d’activité sera consacré à la participation à l’enseignement, sous la responsabilité de l’enseignant·e titulaire. 29% du taux d’activité sera consacré aux travaux de recherche partagés, notamment à la participation aux activités scientifiques de l’unité de recherche et aux activités collectives de recherche. Voir le cahier des charges détaillé. Votre profil Nous souhaitons engager une personne avec le profil suivant : Master en sciences du sport, en biologie ou titre jugé équivalent Intérêt à poursuivre des activités de recherche sur la plasticité de la fonction neuromusculaire Maîtrise du français (obligatoire) et bonnes connaissances de l’anglais Intérêt pour l’enseignement en sciences de la vie Sens de l’organisation, capacité à travailler de façon autonome et indépendante, et au sein d’une équipe de recherche Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié. Des possibilités de formation continue, une multitude d'activités et d'autres avantages à découvrir. Davantage d'informations sur unil.ch/travailler Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Prof. Nicolas Place Nicolas.place@unil.ch Votre dossier de candidature Délai de candidature : 1er octobre 2026 Nous vous prions de bien vouloir nous transmettre les documents ci-dessous en un dossier en format PDF via la plateforme de recrutement : Lettre de motivation, CV académique avec copie des diplômes universitaires et relevés des notes obtenues, Un texte de 1 à 2 pages maximum décrivant les aspects de la plasticité neuromusculaire qui suscitent particulièrement votre intérêt et expliquant les raisons de cet intérêt. Seules les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site seront prises en compte. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie ; •    À soutenir la relève scientifique. unil.ch/egalite unil.ch/familles unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
